152: ## 3. Context Vector Architecture
153: 
154: 17-dimensional feature vector, split into shared (student) and arm-specific (content):
155: 
156: ### Shared Features (z, 8 dims)
157: | Index | Feature | Source |
158: |-------|---------|--------|
159: | 0 | performance_score | Student's overall score (0-1) |
160: | 1 | session_count | log1p(sessions) / log1p(100) |
161: | 2 | grade_trend_slope | Linear regression slope of recent grades |
162: | 3 | education_level | Numeric education level |
163: | 4 | age_band | Numeric age band |
164: | 5 | credits_studied | Credits completed |
165: | 6 | imd_band | Deprivation index (default 0.5) |
166: | 7 | region_code | Numeric region |
167: 
168: ### Arm-Specific Features (x, 9 dims)
169: | Index | Feature | Source |
170: |-------|---------|--------|
171: | 0 | difficulty | (content.difficulty - 1) / 4 |
172: | 1 | topic_match | 1.0 if student topic matches content topic |
173: | 2-5 | content_type | One-hot: video, quiz, exercise, reading |
174: | 6 | perf_diff | performance × difficulty interaction |
175: | 7 | perf_video | performance × video interaction |
176: | 8 | perf_quiz | performance × quiz interaction |
